hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"982","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah bin Unais, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Khalid bin Sufyan bin Nabih al-Hudhali. He was informed that it was being gathered for him, and he was between Arana and Arafat. He said to me: Go and kill him. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, describe him to me. He said: “Then When you saw him, a shiver ran through you. Don’t worry, I will not describe him to you other than this.” He said: And it was. He said: I set off until when I approached him, I was present. Prayer, the afternoon prayer. He said: I said that I was afraid that something would happen to me if I delayed the prayer, so I prayed while I was walking, gesticulating in the same way, and then I finished. To him, by God, as soon as I saw him, I shuddered, and behold, he was in a company of his, that is, in his wives, so I walked with him, and he said: Who are you? I said: An Arab man informed me that you were gathering money for this man, so I came to you about that man, and he said: I am about that one. He said: I said to myself: You will know. He said: So I walked with him for an hour until, if I could, I stabbed him with my sword until he was cold, then I presented Medina to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I told him the news, and he gave me a stick, which he says: a stick, so I took it from him, and my companions said to me: What is this that the Messenger of God gave you? May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I said: Shortened. They said: And what do you do with it? Did you not ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, why he gave you this, and what you do with it? Go back to him and ask him. He said: So I returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, you gave me the summary. Why? He said: “It will be between you and me on the Day of Resurrection, and the least of people on that day will be short-changers.” He said: So he stuck it on his sword, and it would not leave it, but it did not leave it. He was alive, and when death came to him, he ordered us to be buried with him. He said: So, by God, I was placed in his shroud."
"983","Ahmad bin Al-Azhar told us, and I wrote it from its origin. He said: Ya’qub told us, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah bin Unais, on the authority of his father, so he mentioned the hadith in its length. Abu Bakr said: I have included the chapters on the attributes of fear at the end of the Book of Prayer."
